      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The record is a learning — an evidence-backed statement of how code relates to the game, merged from what humans aggregated over the years and what agents pick up along the way. Renamed from 'annotation' (too document-flavored). The graph edge becomes "
        },
        {
          "insert": "HAS_LEARNING",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "; report fields become "
        },
        {
          "insert": "learnings[]",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "learning_verdicts[]",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The corroboration machinery exists precisely because agent-asserted learnings must not be trusted until evidence backs them."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-knowledge-ledger-the-belief-store-is-one-37": {
      "id": "b-10-knowledge-ledger-the-belief-store-is-one-37",
      "type": "quote",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The belief store is ONE ledger with an "
        },
        {
          "insert": "origin",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " field, not two stores: "
        },
        {
          "insert": "origin: \"human_extracted\"",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (a person said it — on Discord or in a PR review — and the extractor transcribed and anchored it) or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "\"ai_inferred\"",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (the AI concluded it by cross-referencing evidence: crosswalk + call edges + wiki sections lining up). Same record shape and lifecycle for both; trust policy differs — human-extracted statements may start at higher confidence and corroborate on a single confirm, ai-inferred ones need the full 2-confirms-or-1-strong bar. Renamed from 'annotations ledger'; the symbol-anchored learning stays the primary record kind, and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "subject",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " may widen to "
        },
        {
          "insert": "symbol | file | area",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for area-level knowledge."
