      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The read contract accepts an append log in which later rows supersede earlier rows with the same ID. The standard writer currently compacts and rewrites the ledger to one latest row per ID, so the live file is a latest snapshot rather than a physical version log. The detail API can return multiple raw versions when such rows exist, but ordinary writes usually leave one."
